				<h2>Solar Only vs. Solar + Battery Storage</h2>
				<p>See why California homeowners are shifting to integrated energy storage systems.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="comparison-grid">
				<!-- Without Battery -->
				<div class="comp-card negative">
					<div class="card-status-pill red">Without Battery Storage</div>
					<h3>Solar Only System</h3>
					<ul class="comp-list">
						<li>❌ <strong>75% Loss on Exported Power:</strong> Daytime solar sold back to PG&E/SCE at wholesale pennies.</li>
						<li>❌ <strong>High Evening Rates:</strong> You still buy expensive peak grid electricity between 4 PM – 9 PM.</li>
						<li>❌ <strong>9–11 Year Payback:</strong> Long payback timeline under NEM 3.0 rules.</li>
						<li>❌ <strong>No Blackout Backup:</strong> System shuts off during grid outages.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<!-- With Battery -->
				<div class="comp-card positive">
					<div class="card-status-pill green">Recommended Choice</div>
					<h3>Solar + Battery System</h3>
					<ul class="comp-list">
						<li>✅ <strong>100% Power Retention:</strong> Store excess daytime solar directly in your battery.</li>
						<li>✅ <strong>Zero Peak Electricity Charges:</strong> Run your home on battery during expensive evening hours.</li>
						<li>✅ <strong>4–6 Year Payback:</strong> Fast ROI driven by high peak-rate avoidance.</li>
