				<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-accordion">
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>How does NEM 3.0 affect solar payback in California?</summary>
					<div class="faq-answer">
						Under NEM 3.0, export credits for power sent back to the grid were cut by roughly 75%. Solar-only systems take 9–11 years to pay off, whereas solar + battery systems pay off in 4–6 years by storing cheap daytime power for expensive evening peak hours.
					</div>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>What is the Federal Tax Credit (ITC) for solar and batteries in 2026?</summary>
					<div class="faq-answer">
						You can claim a 30% federal tax credit on the full installation cost of both solar panels and battery storage systems installed on your primary or secondary residence.
					</div>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>Are standalone batteries eligible for tax credits?</summary>
					<div class="faq-answer">
						Yes! Under current guidelines, standalone battery storage systems (10 kWh or larger) qualify for the 30% federal tax credit even if installed without new solar panels.
					</div>
				</details>
